cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you utilize this computational physics formulation, metrology methodology, or software architecture in your research or technical evaluations, please cite it as indicated below."
title: "NovusMundus: Sutton-Chen Potential in Sobolev H¹, FCC Lattice Metrology, and Idempotent Lakehouse Streaming Architecture"
abstract: "Formal mathematical modeling, computational physics simulation, and quantitative data engineering framework developed by Mikel Irastorza. Establishes the analytical invariant lattice parameter (a = 4.078 Å) under the Sutton-Chen many-body empirical potential in Sobolev H¹ spaces as an absolute atomic metrology standard for Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM) calibration and continuum-to-discrete mechanical tolerance bridging (±0.2 mm sheet metal manufacturing), unified with high-frequency streaming lakehouse pipelines and cryptographically verified state machines."
